======================================================================
(1) H-ENTROPY S_H=log2 H is ADDITIVE over disjoint modules (S531)
======================================================================
  n=8: S_H(A)=1.585, S_H(B)=1.585, S_H(A+B)=3.170; sum=3.170  additive=True
  n=9: S_H(A)=2.322, S_H(B)=2.322, S_H(A+B)=4.644; sum=4.644  additive=True
  apex module size s -> S_H contribution log2(1+2^{s-2}):
    s=2: 1+2^(s-2)=2, log2=1.000
    s=3: 1+2^(s-2)=3, log2=1.585
    s=4: 1+2^(s-2)=5, log2=2.322
    s=5: 1+2^(s-2)=9, log2=3.170
    s=6: 1+2^(s-2)=17, log2=4.087
    s=7: 1+2^(s-2)=33, log2=5.044
  => S_H is a TREE-ADDITIVE entropy: S_H=0 (transitive, rigid) up to log2(H_regular)
     (the regular polygon = LRC-tight extremal). Max entropy = the tight witness.

======================================================================
(1b) H-ENTROPY trajectory S_H(t) over the runner walk, n=5
======================================================================
  AP 1..n (regular)          v=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5): S_H(t) in [0.00,3.91], mean 2.757
  geometric 1,2,4,..         v=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16): S_H(t) in [0.00,3.91], mean 1.926
  random primitive           v=(10, 18, 23, 31, 34): S_H(t) in [0.00,3.91], mean 2.295
  sieve 1,2,..,n with mult   v=(1, 2, 3, 4, 30): S_H(t) in [0.00,3.91], mean 2.576
  PATTERN: max S_H = log2(H_regular) at the spread/regular slices; AP/regular speeds
  carry the HIGHEST mean H-entropy (most time spread) -- entropy fingerprints regularity.

