======================================================================
(2) p-ADIC TREE entropy (p=3): Shannon spread across residues mod p^k
======================================================================
  AP 1..n-1                     : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[1.52, 2.32, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  random primitive              : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[0.72, 1.92, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  sieve: all ≡0 mod p (x3 of 1..): level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[-0.0, 1.52, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  mixed: 1 + multiples of p     : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[0.72, 1.92, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  PATTERN: HIGH tree entropy = speeds spread across channels (debt present, sieve
  blocked, S534 vacuity); LOW entropy / empty 0-branch = sieve loneliness available.

======================================================================
(2) p-ADIC TREE entropy (p=2): Shannon spread across residues mod p^k
======================================================================
  AP 1..n-1                     : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[0.97, 1.92, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  random primitive              : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[0.72, 1.52, 1.92]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  sieve: all ≡0 mod p (x3 of 1..): level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[-0.0, 0.97, 1.92]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  mixed: 1 + multiples of p     : level-entropies(mod p^1..p^3)=[0.72, 1.52, 2.32]; 0-branch empty (sieve t=1/p lonely)=False
  PATTERN: HIGH tree entropy = speeds spread across channels (debt present, sieve
  blocked, S534 vacuity); LOW entropy / empty 0-branch = sieve loneliness available.

======================================================================
(3) ISO-CLASS WALK entropy over t (the menu walk), n=5
======================================================================
  AP 1..n    v=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5): walk entropy=1.825 bits over 4 iso-classes (max if uniform=2.000)
  random     v=(15, 19, 24, 27, 31): walk entropy=1.796 bits over 4 iso-classes (max if uniform=2.000)
  PATTERN: the walk entropy measures the MIXING across the 2Fib(n-2) menu; the
  more uniform the time-in-class, the higher -- another regularity fingerprint.
======================================================================
SYNTHESIS: three TREE entropies all measure SPREAD/MIXING. H-ENTROPY (log2 H) is
TREE-ADDITIVE over the modular tree (S531), maximized at the regular polygon (LRC-
tight). p-adic tree entropy = channel spread (S534): high => sieve blocked. Walk
entropy = menu mixing. Regularity (AP) shows up as HIGH entropy on every tree.
======================================================================
